This project includes, runs or downloads the following third-party software. Each keeps its own license; none of them is changed
here (FieldStation42 is run as it is, and everything else is fetched or installed at build time).

FieldStation42                       https://github.com/shane-mason/FieldStation42
    Mozilla Public License 2.0. A copy of upstream is vendored, unmodified, under fieldstation42/src (its LICENSE is kept there).
    The wrapper changes nothing in it: behaviour is adjusted by fieldstation42/console_launch.py, which wraps a few methods at run
    time. The source of the vendored copy is the upstream repository at the commit named in fieldstation42/FS42_REF.

TA_NFOWriter                         https://github.com/JamesM92/TA_NFOWriter
    MIT License. Downloaded at build time (version and SHA-256 are pinned in the Dockerfile).

mpegts.js                            https://github.com/xqq/mpegts.js
    Apache License 2.0. Downloaded at build time (version and SHA-256 are pinned in the Dockerfile) and served to the web player.

FFmpeg                               https://ffmpeg.org
    LGPL 2.1 or later / GPL 2 or later, depending on the build. Installed from the base image's package repository and run as a
    separate program; it is not linked into this project.

Python packages                      see requirements.txt
    fastapi (MIT), uvicorn (BSD-3-Clause), ffmpeg-python (Apache-2.0), rich (MIT), jsonschema (MIT), requests (Apache-2.0),
    mutagen (GPL-2.0-or-later, used as a separate library for reading audio tags), pillow (HPND), defusedxml (PSF-2.0), and their
    dependencies, each under its own license. They are installed at build time from PyPI.

DejaVu fonts                         https://dejavu-fonts.github.io
    Free license (Bitstream Vera derived), pulled in by the base image's Tk package and used to draw the TV guide channel and channel
    logos.
